---
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL_NAME, MAILING_ADDRESS } from "../site";
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Accessibility statement"
  description="Akimbo Technology's accessibility statement and how to report a barrier."
>
  <p>
    {LEGAL_NAME} wants everyone to be able to use this website, including people who use a
    screen reader, a keyboard instead of a mouse, magnification, or other assistive technology.
  </p>

  <h2>Our target</h2>
  <p>
    We aim for the site to meet the
    <a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/">Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2</a>
    at level AA. We plan to hold the Client Portal at <code>portal.akimbo.technology</code> to the
    same standard.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Pages are built with standard HTML headings, landmarks, lists and form labels.</li>
    <li>
      Every page can be used with a keyboard alone, and a “Skip to content” link is the first
      thing a keyboard user reaches.
    </li>
    <li>We check the contrast of our text and background colour pairs against WCAG AA.</li>
    <li>
      Our contact form doesn’t use a puzzle CAPTCHA. It works without JavaScript, and if sending
      it fails you can email us instead.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Known gaps</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      We check the site by hand, with a keyboard and a screen reader. It has not yet had an
      independent accessibility audit.
    </li>
    <li>
      The contact form uses Cloudflare Turnstile, a third-party service, to stop spam. It
      normally runs without any action from you. If it ever asks you to do something you can’t,
      email us at <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> instead.
    </li>
    <li>
      Documents we send you, such as network audit reports, may not yet be fully accessible. Ask
      us and we will provide them in a format that works for you.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Report a barrier</h2>
  <p>
    If something on the site doesn’t work for you, please tell us. Email
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> with the page address and a short
    description of the problem, or write to us at {LEGAL_NAME}, {MAILING_ADDRESS.join(", ")}.
    We aim to reply within two business days. We’ll also get you the information you need
    another way while we fix the problem.
  </p>

  <h2>About this statement</h2>
  <p>
    We last reviewed this statement on its effective date, shown at the top of this page. We
    review it again whenever the site changes significantly.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
